      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "This article presents a procedure whereby a failed INBONE I saddle talar component and polyethylene insert associated with massive cystic changes within the talus and calcaneus secondary to aseptic osteolysis was treated with impaction cancellous allograft bone graft impregnated with autogenous proximal tibia bone marrow aspirate and conversion to an INBONE II sulcus talar component and polyethylene insert. Concomitantly, a percutaneous tendo-Achilles lengthening and posterior capsule release was performed to enhance ankle dorsiflexion. The rationale for these procedures, the operative sequence of events, and recovery course are presented in detail. Causes for concern regarding subsequent revision, should this be required, are raised."
      },
